WEBVTT

00:01:34.180 --> 00:01:35.720
Squid Girlie!

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:37.320
Who are you?

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.410
Be my husband!

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:40.510
Huh?

00:01:40.510 --> 00:01:42.430
What are you talking about?

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.370
Can't you see I'm a squid?

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:47.210
It's just pretend.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.090
I want you to play house with me.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.510
Play what?

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:58.950
<b>Eel You Play House With Me?!</b>

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:01.280
You don't know what that is?

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:03.430
Just watch me.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:07.090
"Darling, what are these lip-stick stains?!"

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:10.600
"Stop nagging. That happened 
because the train was packed."

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:11.610
"Hmm, I wonder."

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:14.860
"Hey bitch, gimme money.
I'm hitting up the arcade!"

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.270
"I can't live like this anymore!"

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:19.950
What was all that about?

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.330
I guess she has a pretty 
complicated family life...

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:24.720
Do you get it now?

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:25.480
Yes!

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:29.830
This is a game where you become 
father, mother, and kids.

00:02:29.830 --> 00:02:31.530
That's right!

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.280
I'll be the mom and you be the dad.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.550
Okay!

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.260
Honey,

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:40.370
is everything all right at work?

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:42.220
Yes. Everything's going well.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.620
At this rate, by next week I'll have 
invaded 80 percent of the world.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.670
Invaded?

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.440
Here you are, Squid Girl!

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:53.230
I'm not Squid Girl right now.
 I'm Squid Man!

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.140
Huh?

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.940
What the heck have you gotten into?

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:58.440
You want to play house with us, too?

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:00.780
You're playing house?

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.410
Who is this little girl, anyway?

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:06.150
I'll play the little girl. 
Why don't you be the mom?

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:07.950
I... I actually think I'll pass.

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.290
Daddy! You're home!

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.310
I'm back!

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:14.140
They're not giving me much choice.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:18.840
Hi, Honey!

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.220
Would you like your bath first, 
or your dinner first, or-

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:23.640
I want shrimp!

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.600
You're the only one!

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:31.020
Chizuru told me they were 
at the park, but where?

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:32.390
Is that...

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:34.490
Open wide...

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:37.320
Eiko!

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.170
What the hell is this?!

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.090
Sanae!

00:03:40.090 --> 00:03:41.720
That's my job!

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.350
How dare you?!

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:44.570
Calm down!

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:44.570
Who is that?

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:45.650
My arch-nemesis.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:46.330
Arch-nemesis?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:50.100
How can you do this when you 
know how I feel about Squiddie?

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:54.210
Playing house means simulating married life!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.490
You think I'm going to just let that pass?

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:59.510
You're hurting me. Let go!

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.610
Want to play house with us, too?

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:04.300
You can play Squid Dad's illicit lover!

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:07.260
Where did this kid learn this stuff?

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:10.140
Squiddie's illicit lover...

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:14.310
I'm home!

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:16.000
Hi, Daddy!

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.480
Hello, honey!

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.590
And just who is that woman behind you?!

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:21.770
Behind me?

00:04:21.770 --> 00:04:23.450
When did you get here?

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:28.340
You've always refused to
 tell me your address,

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:31.830
so I just followed you all
 the way home from work.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.340
She would, too.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.620
What's the meaning of this?

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:37.610
You better have a good explanation!

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:39.210
Well... it's that...

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:41.310
Isn't it obvious?

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:43.300
Squid Man and I are in love.

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.720
Let's retreat to our love nest!

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.350
No!

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:50.970
This is no different from 
any other day, huh?

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.750
Let me go!

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:53.930
Squiddie!

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:56.050
Kiyomi!

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:59.770
You never smile at me like that!

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.220
Let's make this clear once and for all!

00:05:02.220 --> 00:05:03.110
Make what clear, exactly?

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:04.390
Don't play stupid!

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:06.950
I know you two are always hanging out!

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.470
That's because of our 
Invasion Club activities!

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:11.580
Would you like to become a member, too?

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:15.290
Like I'd join a club my rival's a member of!

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:16.500
Rival?

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:20.440
Let's make it clear who really loves Squiddie!

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:22.960
A love triangle has developed! 
This is awesome!

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:25.920
Again, where did she learn all these things?

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.410
Want to play house, too?

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.510
Oh, so that's what this is.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:33.350
You can play my Daddy's latest lover!

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:34.810
L-lover?!

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.770
It looks like her home has oceans of drama.

00:05:38.470 --> 00:05:41.730
I don't know how good 
I'll be at it, but I can try.

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:44.820
So you're Squid Man's new lover, huh?!

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.210
Yes.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:46.930
My name is Kiyomi.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:47.910
Nice to meet you.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.800
She... smiled.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.370
Someone who can smile 
there has real talent.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:56.060
Squid Man is the type who's 
easily dazzled by new things,

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:59.520
but you know that old saying: 
"Lovers and tatami mats are best old!"

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:03.230
I think that saying is 
"Lovers and tatami mats are best new."

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:05.130
You're both wrong. 
It's "wives" and "tatami mats."

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:09.880
So are you saying I should 
be with my squidtastic lover Kiyomi,

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:14.520
or should I squid unto Eiko, 
since she's my wife?

00:06:15.820 --> 00:06:19.230
Eiko's done so much for me, 
but Kiyomi's my friend...

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:21.740
Of course, you should choose me, Squid Man.

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:23.940
No squidding way.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:26.400
I don't think this is a game of house anymore.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:30.110
I can't live without you anymore, Squid Man!

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:32.830
Let's go to our love nest!

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.200
No! No!

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.290
I told you, no!

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.830
Shouldn't we stop her?

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.090
That would just complicate things.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:42.920
Huh? What?

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.850
Untentacle me!

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.760
You said you were going to 
have a baby, didn't you?

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:49.470
A b-b-baby?

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.180
She wanted it to be complicated?

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.830
How could you do this to me, Squiddie?!

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:57.600
You'd only have to say the word, 
and I'd gladly have your baby!

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:00.060
She would, too.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:05.070
You keep talking about babies, 
but whose baby, squidxactly?

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:06.620
You can't play dumb, Daddy!

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:09.140
Me and Mommy saw the maternity record book!

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:09.730
Didn't we?

00:07:09.730 --> 00:07:11.870
You know about that stuff too?!

00:07:11.870 --> 00:07:13.540
Yeah, we saw it!

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.130
It said you're in the final month,

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:16.910
so you have to give birth, right?

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:20.850
I will give birth to this baby,
 even if I have to do it alone!!

00:07:21.560 --> 00:07:22.880
Daddy, what are you going to do?

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:24.380
Honey!

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:24.380
Squiddie!

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.920
Can't we talk about it?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.460
You good-for-nothing!

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:32.300
You're... you're not my daddy!

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:36.680
Rampaging horses are loose in the street!

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.890
You're in the street now?

00:07:38.890 --> 00:07:39.890
Watch out!

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.440
Squid Girl, are you all right?

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:47.160
You can't die, Daddy!

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:48.230
Honey!

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:50.190
Don't leave me here all alone, Squid Man!

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.150
I shall die as well, Squid Man!

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:56.080
Please... squidvade the surface... for me.

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:59.060
Squid Man!

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:59.060
Honey!

00:07:56.420 --> 00:07:59.060
Daddy!

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:02.150
That was great!

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:03.680
Thank you, girls!

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:04.900
Bye bye!

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:06.040
Bye bye!

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:07.410
Take care!

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.320
You were 90 percent serious.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:10.550
That's a lie!

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.070
I was 100 percent serious!

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:13.010
I thought so.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:17.720
Makes you wonder what squeird 
kind of house Risa is being raised in.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:21.480
Stop this madness!

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:24.440
I'll kill you first and then myself!

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.360
Stop! We can still talk about this!

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:28.550
Turn that off already.

00:08:29.720 --> 00:08:33.030
You sure love those love-hate dramas.

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:39.770
I bought this bag, but it's too big

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:42.270
and there's never a chance to use it.

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:47.380
I bought this planner,
 but I never use it.

00:08:49.390 --> 00:08:50.660
Here, Squid Girl.

00:08:50.660 --> 00:08:51.860
You can have this.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:53.420
And this.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:54.680
It's a bag.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.510
This is a planner.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:58.330
What is that for?

00:08:58.330 --> 00:09:01.010
You use this to write down your appointments.

00:09:01.010 --> 00:09:04.080
Not that you ever have those, though.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:07.520
There's nothing I can't squidding use.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:12.530
<b>Didn't We Have A Squidrrangement?!</b>

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:13.260
Work

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:13.360
Food

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:13.570
Food
Bath, TV

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:13.780
Food
Bath, TV
Gaming

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:15.490
I guess that does it.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.490
Food
Bath, TV
Gaming
Sleep

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.370
There's nothing else to ink here.

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.990
I'm sure I can make exsquidlent use of this bag.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:26.750
I'm already done.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:30.850
I don't feel like I'm using this right.

00:09:30.850 --> 00:09:32.500
Squiddie?

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:33.950
Kiyomi!

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:36.030
What's that bag for?

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:37.830
I got it from Chizuru.

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:41.340
I'm not quite sure what 
I should put in it, though.

00:09:41.340 --> 00:09:44.020
What do you have in your bag?

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:46.220
I've got my towel, a water bottle, and such.

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:48.570
You know, stuff I need for my club.

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:50.120
Can I take a squiddle peek?

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:50.730
Sure.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:54.020
Today, I've only got my club, 
so this is all that's in there,

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:55.280
but when I've got class,

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:57.420
I put my textbooks and 
notebooks in there, too.

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.900
I get it!

00:09:58.900 --> 00:10:01.870
You put in the things you'll 
need while you're out.

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:02.910
Yeah!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:05.830
You've got a big bag, so you could 
fit pretty much anything in there.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:08.120
A planner!

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:10.770
Can I look at this, too?

00:10:10.770 --> 00:10:12.040
Okay.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:15.690
Wow, you've got so much stuff to ink in!

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.760
I'm so jealous.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:19.170
You could write down

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:21.260
the things you have to get 
done at the restaurant.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:22.710
You're right!

00:10:22.710 --> 00:10:24.220
I'm going to do that right now.

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:26.180
Lemon

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.330
What's that?

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.400
Hey, you should ask before 
you just take my clock!

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:37.360
It's time to prepare for opening.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:43.660
You're not done with the refilling yet!

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.870
I can't help it, I'm following the plan.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:47.830
What plan?

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:50.620
8.30 Refill soy sauce
8.45 Opening preparations
Put chairs down with tentac-
8.55 Bathroom

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:54.000
You've got that planned out to the minute.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:55.470
I'll have a sardine rice bowl.

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:56.260
And I'll have a Yokohama ramen.

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:59.010
A sardine rice bowl. A Yokohama ramen...

00:11:02.150 --> 00:11:03.300
What are you doing?

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:07.420
Hey!

00:11:07.420 --> 00:11:09.050
What about our order?

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:12.600
10.20 Hydration

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:15.430
I have to drink water before I get dehydrated, 
or there's no point.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:17.690
You're in the middle of waiting on customers!

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.330
Twelve o'clock. 
Time for lunch.

00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:28.790
Chizuru!

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.290
I'd like shrimp fried rice for lunch, please.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.500
You shouldn't walk around 
with raw stuff in your bag!

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:36.250
Anyway, you can eat your lunch later!

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:37.360
Take this out.

00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:39.190
That's going to squid up my plan.

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:40.670
NOW!

00:11:44.070 --> 00:11:45.820
Three o'clock. Snack time.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:49.420
How the squid can it be snack time already, 
when I haven't even had lunch?

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:53.240
I'm sorry, but could you run 
out and buy some cabbages?

00:11:53.240 --> 00:11:54.600
But it's my snack time...

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.800
You can buy a snack too, 
just please go!

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:58.190
I guess that works.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:01.270
Good thing I brought my wallet.

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:04.000
What "wallet"?!

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.110
This is my piggy bank!

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:07.410
Squid Girlie, come quick!

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:10.660
We were playing volleyball and 
our ball got carried out on the tide!

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.000
Do I have to go right now?

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:13.750
Water, please.

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:14.800
Yes!

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:16.060
You're still here?

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.260
I need those cabbages right away!

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.980
What the squid should I do?

00:12:20.980 --> 00:12:24.030
Should I get my snack first, or the cabbages,

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:26.310
or rescue Takeru from the tide?

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:27.720
I'm right here.

00:12:28.670 --> 00:12:29.820
You're panicking.

00:12:29.820 --> 00:12:31.870
Squiddie!

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:34.410
Huh?

00:12:34.410 --> 00:12:36.060
It's Sanae!

00:12:37.970 --> 00:12:38.860
Huh?

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:40.940
I could've sworn I just saw Squiddie.

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:44.950
I'll be back.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.340
Is she gone?

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:48.270
Yes.

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:53.440
3:10.

00:12:53.440 --> 00:12:54.080
Bathroom.

00:12:55.550 --> 00:12:58.590
My plans aren't squidding 
working out at all!

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.000
What did I tell you?

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:05.150
How can I make my plans all fit together?

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:06.510
Squiddie.

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:07.780
Kiyomi!

00:13:07.780 --> 00:13:08.700
How's it going?

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.280
Are you getting the hang of 
your bag and your planner?

00:13:11.840 --> 00:13:13.620
I keep making all these plans,

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.400
but then these other things 
come up and nothing works out.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:17.780
That happens to me, too.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:20.360
See?

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:25.450
Club (gym)
Return books (library)

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:23.740
I was supposed to go to the 
library after my club,

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:25.450
but I'm really tired,
so I'm going home instead.

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:28.220
After all, plans are just plans.

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:32.450
So you're saying it's okay 
to not follow the plan?

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.660
Not exactly.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:38.130
Then I'm going to plan with all my heart!

00:13:38.690 --> 00:13:39.960
Today's plan:

00:13:40.330 --> 00:13:42.210
Seven o'clock, Aizawa house,

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:43.420
commence invasion.

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:44.760
Ten o'clock.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:46.510
Defeat Chizuru.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:47.890
Seven at night.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:49.760
Invade Kantou!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.140
Eight at night.

00:13:51.140 --> 00:13:53.080
Invade Western Japan.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:53.520
You won this battle!
Motonari Mori has committed suicide.
The Mori family has fallen.

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:54.850
Ten at night.

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:57.980
Complete invasion of Japan.

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:57.980
Complete invasion of Japan.

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:01.020
You're not following your planner at all.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:03.120
Plans are supposed to be flexible.

00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:04.960
Yeah, but only to a certain point.

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:08.030
Would you like to unwind this weekend 
from your hard week at work?

00:14:08.050 --> 00:14:10.160
<b>Weekend hotspot!
Hakone Yuno-Oni Hot Springs</b>

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:10.160
Then come to the Hakone 
Yuno-Oni Hot Springs!

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:11.930
Hot springs, huh?

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:14.870
Sure, why the squid not? 
I've finished invading.

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:16.580
Hakone
Yuno-Oni Hot springs

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:16.580
You're not done at all!

00:14:16.940 --> 00:14:18.850
Hey, let's play!

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:19.970
Sure.

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.730
Bye!

00:14:23.730 --> 00:14:25.060
Bye bye!

00:14:29.770 --> 00:14:30.760
Hi, Sanae.

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:32.190
Here.

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:33.830
This is that CD I was talking about.

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:34.810
Thank you.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.560
Oh, and... I found this in front of the door.

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:39.420
Hey, that's Squid Girl's!

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:40.500
Thanks.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:42.370
My pleasure.

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:45.820
An amusement park?

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:46.910
Yeah!

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.050
I was thinking we could all go next weekend.

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:50.800
Wow. I've never heard

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:53.230
of a place like that before, 
but it sounds like waves of fun.

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:53.990
--Hot--Springs--
Amusement Park

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.270
I wonder when Squiddie will get here.

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:00.900
I'm getting light-headed...

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.760
Thank you for riding with us.

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:10.060
Hurry up!

00:15:10.060 --> 00:15:11.390
We'll miss the next train!

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.760
We're fine.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.350
Everyone, sit down, squidmediately!

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.790
Stop freaking out! 
The train is empty.

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:24.900
You don't have to rush, Squid Girlie.

00:15:24.900 --> 00:15:26.780
The amusement park isn't going anywhere.

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:31.780
<b>Shall We Jet Over To An Amusement Park?!</b>

00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.510
I haven't been there in so long.

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:35.030
Yeah!

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.370
I think I was in grade school the last time.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:41.960
So what kind of place is 
an amusement park, anyway?

00:15:43.180 --> 00:15:46.670
You were sure hurrying a lot for someone 
who doesn't even know what it is.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:50.010
An amusement park is where a lot of

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:52.380
things are spinning around...

00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:53.760
Spinning...

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:56.130
Squiddie... Squiddie!

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:58.140
And where things zoom out at you!

00:15:59.920 --> 00:16:01.770
And things rattle you around.

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.270
Rattle, rattle...

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:05.730
Squiddie!

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:08.200
It sounds terrifying!

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.400
<b>Dream Amusement Park</b>

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:12.920
Wow, it's been forever!

00:16:12.920 --> 00:16:15.280
The sign's just like it was back then!

00:16:15.630 --> 00:16:17.630
Squid Girlie, it's fine.

00:16:17.630 --> 00:16:19.240
This is a fun place.

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:22.410
This place hasn't changed one bit.

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:25.040
Here, I bought our access passes.

00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:28.130
Oh, they've got those now.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:28.130
Access Pass
800 Yen

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:30.090
How lame...! 
And they charge 800 yen?!

00:16:30.330 --> 00:16:32.530
Let's go, Squid Girlie!

00:16:32.530 --> 00:16:34.050
All right, all right!

00:16:36.290 --> 00:16:38.970
They've only got the coffee cup ride?

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:42.370
That's the recession for you.

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:43.940
It's the ticket seller.

00:16:43.940 --> 00:16:47.640
Guests stopped coming, 
so our revenue went down,

00:16:47.640 --> 00:16:50.350
then we couldn't pay our 
employees anymore.

00:16:50.350 --> 00:16:53.900
But we wanted this amusement 
park to survive.

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.360
We sold the land off bit 
by bit until we ended up

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:58.000
with what you see now.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:00.370
It's a tough world we live in.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:02.790
But you're lucky.

00:17:03.390 --> 00:17:06.950
This is the park's last day.

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:07.850
What?

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:09.090
Really?

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:12.830
I don't mind if this park disappears,

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:16.270
so long as it lives on in your memories.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:21.430
We're going to stay with you, 
pops, to the bitter end!

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:22.890
That's right!

00:17:22.890 --> 00:17:25.170
Let's ride the heck out 
of these coffee cups!

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:26.190
Agreed!

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:29.770
Thank you so much.

00:17:32.930 --> 00:17:35.400
You were right, these really do spin!

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:38.730
It zooms at you, and you even rattle!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:42.410
I think I meant it a little differently.

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:51.140
I can't... anymore...

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:52.380
These are rough....

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:54.950
I'm getting really sick.

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:57.840
I'm completely fine.

00:17:58.230 --> 00:17:59.850
Round and round and round we go!

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:03.990
Looks like Squid Girl's 
really enjoying this.

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:07.230
She's really good at that.

00:18:07.750 --> 00:18:10.800
I said we'd stay here all day,

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:12.990
but that's going to be harder than I thought.

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:16.020
Excuse me?

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:18.660
When does this park close?

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:22.530
Eleven... at night?

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:23.490
That long?!

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:27.500
We've got to keep up with Mouseland 
since they stay open late, too.

00:18:27.500 --> 00:18:28.460
It's you!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.910
You've got a weird sense of pride

00:18:30.910 --> 00:18:32.920
for someone who only has 
the coffee cup ride.

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:35.490
I guess you're right.

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:37.440
There's no reason for an amusement park

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:39.890
with only the coffee cup ride to exist.

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:42.370
It would be better for everyone

00:18:42.370 --> 00:18:45.540
if we just went away, once and for all.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.080
Oh, come on!

00:18:47.080 --> 00:18:48.850
Isn't that taking it a little too far?

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:51.840
The coffee cup ride is really fun!

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:55.110
If anything, the coffee cup ride 
is the soul of an amusement park!

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:58.220
That's all well to say, 
but how are we going

00:18:58.220 --> 00:19:00.240
to kill over ten more hours here?

00:19:00.240 --> 00:19:03.240
Now let's spin the other way!

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:06.820
Damn, she's totally fine.

00:19:06.820 --> 00:19:09.560
Is there really nothing else 
besides the coffee cups?

00:19:09.560 --> 00:19:12.110
Some kind of game or anything...

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:17.760
10 Yen

00:19:16.870 --> 00:19:17.760
That's so cheap!

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:24.320
Well, I guess it beats the coffee cups.

00:19:32.630 --> 00:19:34.120
It stops too soon!

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:35.860
Just make the damn fee 100 yen!

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:47.700
I barely did anything today, 
but I'm still so exhausted.

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:49.040
Hey!

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:51.170
Does anyone want to go
 for a squiddle spin with me?

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:53.690
Takeru, will you ride with her?

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:55.420
No.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:59.700
I don't think I'll ever ride that ride again.

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:01.630
He's been traumatized.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:06.310
But in an hour, it'll be over for good, I guess.

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:10.020
Kind of sad when you think of it like that.

00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:30.120
What are you getting all teary eyed about?

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:33.910
It's not like you've got any 
regrets about this place.

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:44.190
I can't manage a parade, 
but I can at least create the mood.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:50.980
Fireworks!

00:20:52.790 --> 00:20:54.280
They're so beautiful!

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.260
Yeah!

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:01.030
I guess it's not a bad way to go out.

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:08.490
Effective immediately, 
this park shuts its doors completely.

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:12.410
Thanks so much for staying 
with me to the end.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:15.100
The coffee cups were so much fun!

00:21:15.100 --> 00:21:16.130
Yeah...

00:21:16.130 --> 00:21:18.490
Especially the first ten minutes...

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:20.180
Goodbye!

00:21:20.180 --> 00:21:21.420
Take care!

00:21:21.420 --> 00:21:22.840
Take care, pops!

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:38.600
I wonder what they'll do with this property?

00:21:38.600 --> 00:21:40.190
Yeah, I wonder.

00:21:40.510 --> 00:21:42.820
But we'll always remember it.

00:21:43.520 --> 00:21:44.850
That's good enough.

00:21:51.150 --> 00:21:55.300
It looks like they remodeled 
that amusement park!

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:57.330
Really? And the old man?

00:21:58.540 --> 00:22:00.200
It's great that he found a new job.

00:22:00.200 --> 00:22:01.640
Good for him!

00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:08.150
Well, the old guy sure 
killed that memory for me.

00:23:40.550 --> 00:23:44.120
Oh, hello. My name's Chizuru Aizawa.

00:23:44.120 --> 00:23:45.050
Next up are:

00:23:45.050 --> 00:23:46.280
Squid meets grill?!

00:23:46.280 --> 00:23:47.550
Wanna learn self-squidfense?!

00:23:47.550 --> 00:23:48.780
Aren't you freezing your tentacles off?!

00:23:48.780 --> 00:23:52.950
Please enjoy them. 
No need to be modest about it.
